# DCA drift-alert Slack webhook — environment template.
#
# The drift detector (scripts/drift_detection.py) reads the Slack incoming-webhook
# URL at runtime from the DCA_DRIFT_SLACK_WEBHOOK environment variable. The URL is
# a secret: anyone who has it can post to your Slack channel, so it must NEVER be
# committed to git.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file to deploy/drift-slack.env (that path is gitignored):
#        cp deploy/drift-slack.env.example deploy/drift-slack.env
#   2. Replace the placeholder below with your real webhook URL.
#   3. Load it before running the detector, or point systemd/cron at it — see
#      docs/slack_webhook_injection.md for the per-runtime setup (cron/systemd,
#      external agent/MCP scheduler, local shell, and GitHub Actions).
#
# NEVER commit deploy/drift-slack.env or paste a real webhook into any tracked file.

DCA_DRIFT_SLACK_WEBHOOK=REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REAL_WEBHOOK_URL

# Optional: uncomment and set this if your deployment relocates the artifact
# tree outside the checkout (dca_paths.stream_root() honors this per
# AGENTS.md:20). The cron/systemd templates in deploy/ source this same file,
# so setting it here also points their run-directory lookup at the right root
# (codex review discussion_r3697136664).
#DCA_CRON_TRACKING_ROOT=/path/to/cron_tracking
